index=streamfwd sourcetype="stream:icmp"
| eventstats values(type_string) as icmp_types by flow_id
| eval has_echo_reply=if(mvfind(icmp_types,"Echo Reply")>=0,1,0)
| eval has_echo_request=if(mvfind(icmp_types,"Echo")>=0
    AND mvfind(icmp_types,"Echo Reply")<0,1,0)


### Rule Description

This rule identifies ICMP flows containing Echo Reply messages without corresponding Echo Request messages within the same `flow_id`. 
This pattern may indicate ICMP reflection activity associated with a potential Smurf attack, in which ICMP traffic is used to overwhelm a target with responses.
The rule groups ICMP events by `flow_id` and flags flows where Echo Reply traffic is observed without a corresponding Echo Request. 
Further investigation of traffic volume, source and destination IP addresses, and repeated responses is recommended to determine whether the activity is malicious.

**Note:** This detection pattern alone does not confirm a Smurf attack and may generate false positives in environments where only one direction of ICMP traffic is captured.
